  "summary": "Traditional storage containers made by steaming and bending a single plank of wood into a box shape.",
  "description": "These boxes feature distinctive formline painting and are crafted by steaming a cedar plank until pliable, then bending it into a rectangular shape with corner joints. They serve practical storage purposes while also functioning as important cultural objects that convey family crests and stories.",
